<h2 class="bde-heading-506-128 bde-heading">
Why Is Max Strus Paid $16.66m After His Trade?
</h2><div class="bde-fancy-container-506-129 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-fancy-container-506-145 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-f-text-506-158 bde-f-text">
<p>Strus is paid <strong>$16.66m</strong> because he shoots from distance in volume and a club over the cap has to pay that price to acquire it.</p>
<ul>
<li>He has made more than 200 three pointers in a season and shot close to 40% doing it.</li>
<li>He went undrafted and his first four years paid him under <strong>$4m</strong> in total.</li>
<li>He tore a cruciate ligament in his first game for <a href="/teams/chicago-bulls/">Chicago</a> in 2019, which cost him a season.</li>
<li>The contract was signed as a sign-and-trade, which is how a club with no cap space gets a free agent it wants.</li>
<li>He turns 31 in March, and this is the last guaranteed year he has.</li>
</ul>
<p>His first NBA season paid him <strong>$415k</strong>. This one pays forty times that.</p>

</div><div class="bde-shortcode-506-159 bde-shortcode"><div class="nba-fin" data-nba-fin="why">
